    "['set interfaces [interface_name]', [{'para_map': [], 'trans_command': 'interface GigabitEthernet0/0/1', 'parent_command': [], 'root': 'interface GigabitEthernet0/0/1', 'source': 'llm', 'origin_reponse': 'Here\\'s the equivalent Cisco configuration for the given Juniper commands:\\n\\n##\\ninterface GigabitEthernet0/0/1\\n ip address 11.1.1.1 255.255.255.0\\n mpls ip\\n##\\n\\nThe translation includes:\\n1. Changing the interface naming convention from Juniper\\'s ge-0/0/1 to Cisco\\'s GigabitEthernet0/0/1\\n2. Converting the CIDR notation (/24) to dotted decimal subnet mask (255.255.255.0)\\n3. Enabling MPLS on the interface with \"mpls ip\" command\\n4. The unit 0 concept is implicit in Cisco and doesn\\'t need explicit configuration', 'trans_template': 'interface GigabitEthernet0/0/1'}, {'para_map': [], 'trans_command': 'ip address 11.1.1.1 255.255.255.0', 'parent_command': [], 'root': 'ip address 11.1.1.1 255.255.255.0', 'source': 'llm', 'origin_reponse': 'Here\\'s the equivalent Cisco configuration for the given Juniper commands:\\n\\n##\\ninterface GigabitEthernet0/0/1\\n ip address 11.1.1.1 255.255.255.0\\n mpls ip\\n##\\n\\nThe translation includes:\\n1. Changing the interface naming convention from Juniper\\'s ge-0/0/1 to Cisco\\'s GigabitEthernet0/0/1\\n2. Converting the CIDR notation (/24) to dotted decimal subnet mask (255.255.255.0)\\n3. Enabling MPLS on the interface with \"mpls ip\" command\\n4. The unit 0 concept is implicit in Cisco and doesn\\'t need explicit configuration', 'trans_template': 'ip address 11.1.1.1 255.255.255.0'}, {'para_map': [], 'trans_command': 'mpls ip', 'parent_command': [], 'root': 'interface [parameter1]', 'source': 'llm', 'origin_reponse': 'Here\\'s the equivalent Cisco configuration for the given Juniper commands:\\n\\n##\\ninterface GigabitEthernet0/0/1\\n ip address 11.1.1.1 255.255.255.0\\n mpls ip\\n##\\n\\nThe translation includes:\\n1. Changing the interface naming convention from Juniper\\'s ge-0/0/1 to Cisco\\'